 </svg></div></div></div></a></div></div></div><div class="navigation-overlay"></div></div><main class="main"><section class="section page-header"><div class="w-layout-blockcontainer container w-container"><div class="w-layout-vflex section-content"><div class="w-layout-vflex text center narrow" data-gsap-scroll="text"><h1 class="heading-h1">Help</h1><div class="text-medium">This page explains how the template works under the hood — every custom system, every animation, every technical decision.</div></div></div></div></section><section class="section padding-top-extra-small"><div class="w-layout-blockcontainer container sticky w-container"><div class="w-layout-vflex section-content"><div class="sidebar-layout" data-pin-wrap="true"><div class="sidebar sticky" data-gsap-scroll="fade" id="w-node-_3e3c1105-280a-78d1-39de-36fd39a4d0e6-ff1718e4"><div class="anchor-nav"><a class="anchor-nav-item w-inline-block" href="#overview"><div class="text-medium">01</div><div class="text-medium">Overview</div></a><a class="anchor-nav-item w-inline-block" href="#infinity-marquee"><div class="text-medium">02</div><div class="text-medium">GSAP Marquee</div></a><a class="anchor-nav-item w-inline-block" href="#gsap-interactions"><div class="text-medium">03</div><div class="text-medium">GSAP Interactions</div></a><a class="anchor-nav-item w-inline-block" href="#light-dark"><div class="text-medium">04</div><div class="text-medium">Light and Dark</div></a><a class="anchor-nav-item w-inline-block" href="#icons-logos"><div class="text-medium">05</div><div class="text-medium">SVG Icons and Logos</div></a><a class="anchor-nav-item w-inline-block" href="#removing-effects"><div class="text-medium">06</div><div class="text-medium">Removing Effects</div></a><a class="anchor-nav-item w-inline-block" href="#best-practices"><div class="text-medium">07</div><div class="text-medium">Best Practices</div></a><a class="anchor-nav-item w-inline-block" href="#infinity-slider"><div class="text-medium">08</div><div class="text-medium">Infinite Slider (Optional)</div></a><a class="anchor-nav-item w-inline-block" href="#smooth-scroll"><div class="text-medium">09</div><div class="text-medium">Smooth Scroll </div></a></div></div><div class="sidebar-slides" data-gsap-scroll="stagger"><div class="sidebar-slide"><div class="heading-h6">The template combines native Webflow components with a small, carefully selected set of custom systems: marquees, GSAP-powered scroll animations, and a variable-mode-driven dark section system. Optional add-ons — smooth scrolling and infinite slider looping — are included as paste-in snippets in their respective sections. Everything is designed to stay editable in the Designer.</div></div><div class="w-layout-vflex sidebar-slide" id="overview"><div class="stack gap-06" id="data"><h2 class="heading-h5">Overview</h2><div class="text-medium">The template ships with a small set of custom scripts and a single global stylesheet. Everything lives either in the project's <strong>global head/footer code</strong> or in <strong>page-level custom code</strong>. Nothing is injected at runtime.</div></div><div class="stack gap-06" id="data"><h3 class="heading-h6">What is included</h3><div class="w-richtext"><ul role="list"><li><strong>GSAP Marquee</strong> — simple GSAP loop for horizontal scrolling content, both directions.</li><li><strong>GSAP Scroll Interactions</strong> — built inside Webflow Interactions, triggered by data attributes.</li><li><strong>Font Smoothing</strong> — minimal global font-smoothing declarations.</li></ul></div></div><div class="stack gap-06" id="data"><h3 class="heading-h6">Optional add-ons</h3><div class="w-richtext"><ul role="list"><li><strong>Lenis Smooth Scroll</strong> — paste-in snippet, integrates with the GSAP ticker.</li><li><strong>Infinite Slider</strong> — paste-in snippet that adds seamless looping to the native Webflow slider.</li></ul></div></div><div class="stack gap-06" id="data"><h3 class="heading-h6">Required libraries</h3><div class="text-medium">The template assumes <strong>GSAP</strong> and <strong>ScrollTrigger</strong> are loaded globally before any of the custom scripts run.</div></div><div class="stack gap-06" id="data"><h3 class="heading-h6">Where the code lives</h3><div class="text-medium">Open <em>Site Settings → Custom Code</em> to find the global scripts.</div></div></div><div class="w-layout-vflex sidebar-slide" id="infinity-marquee"><div class="stack gap-06" id="data"><h2 class="heading-h5">GSAP Marquee</h2><div class="text-medium">The template uses a simple GSAP loop to create horizontal marquees moving in either direction. The animation runs on any element with a <code>data-marquee</code> attribute.</div></div><div class="stack gap-06" id="data"><h3 class="heading-h6">What it does</h3><div class="w-richtext"><p>Build the marquee content as a single horizontal track that contains your items <strong>duplicated once</strong> — so the loop can travel the full width of the original set and then snap back invisibly. Add one of these attributes to the track:</p><ul role="list"><li><code>data-marquee="left"</code> — moves right to left.</li><li><code>data-marquee="right"</code> — moves left to right.</li></ul></div></div><div class="stack gap-06" id="data"><h3 class="heading-h6">Tuning</h3><div class="w-richtext"><ul role="list"><li><strong>Speed</strong> — change the <code>duration</code> value. Higher = slower. Lower = faster.</li><li><strong>Direction</strong> — pick the attribute that matches the direction you want.</li><li><strong>Why -50%</strong> — because the track contains the item set duplicated, moving by half its width loops back to the visually identical starting point.</li></ul></div></div><div class="stack gap-06" id="data"><h3 class="heading-h6">The script</h3><pre class="code-block w-code-block" contenteditable="false" style="display:block;overflow-x:auto;background:#fefefe;color:#545454;padding:0.5em"><code class="language-javascript" style="white-space:pre-wrap"><span><span>&lt;script&gt;
 </span></span><span><span>  gsap.to(</span><span style="color:#008000">'[data-marquee="left"]'</span><span>, {
@@ -329,11 +341,11 @@
 </span></span><span>  });
 </span><span>
 </span><span><span class="xml javascript">  gsap.ticker.lagSmoothing(</span><span class="xml javascript" style="color:#aa5d00">0</span><span class="xml javascript">);
-</span></span><span><span class="xml javascript"></span><span class="xml" style="color:#d91e18">&lt;/</span><span class="xml" style="color:#d91e18">script</span><span class="xml" style="color:#d91e18">&gt;</span></span></code></pre></div><div class="stack gap-06" id="data"><h3 class="heading-h6">How to remove</h3><div class="text-medium">Delete the script block. The page returns to native browser scrolling. ScrollTrigger and all GSAP animations continue to work normally — no other changes needed.</div></div></div></div></div></div></div></section></main><section class="section cta"><div class="w-layout-blockcontainer container w-container"><div class="w-layout-vflex cta-content"><div class="w-layout-vflex text center narrow" data-gsap-scroll="text"><h2 class="heading-h2">For teams preparing for <em>growth</em>, not hype</h2></div><div class="w-layout-vflex buttons" data-gsap-scroll="fade"><a class="button-primary animated w-inline-block" href="https://108.supply/website/people-work?utm_source=people-work&amp;utm_medium=template&amp;utm_campaign=get-template" target="_blank"><div class="button-label" data-figma-id="12018:4671">Get Template</div><div class="button-rail"><div class="button-circle small accent"><div class="icon small w-embed"><svg fill="none" viewbox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
