do not store secrets, tokens, passwords, or credentials living inside your work. Unless you explicitly allow access, your full repositories remain exactly where you left them. From time to time we may store anonymized performance data to improve accuracy and reliability, but this data cannot be traced back to you, your company, or your questionable folder naming conventions.</div></div></div><div class="sidebar-slide" id="informations"><div class="stack gap-06"><h2 class="heading-h5">2. How We Use Your Information</h2><div class="text-medium">Your data is used for one reason only: to make People Work work. That means generating structured insights, creating explanations, supporting documentation flows, and improving the overall quality of the system. <br/><br/>Your information is never used to train public AI models and never leaves isolated systems dedicated to your account. We may look at aggregated, anonymous trends to improve the product. For example, if a surprising number of users struggle with a specific pattern, we improve detection. If everyone struggles to fully understand the 108™ System, we accept that as a natural law of the universe. Even Ariel admits that something can be simple and still confusing, especially when he designed it himself.</div></div></div><div class="w-layout-vflex sidebar-slide" id="protection"><div class="stack gap-06"><h2 class="heading-h5">3. How Your Data is Stored &amp; Protected</h2><div class="text-medium">All data is encrypted both in transit and at rest using modern industry standards. Access to production systems is limited to essential team members and protected by role based permissions, logging, and internal reviews. Backups are handled carefully and stored in secure, geographically separated environments. Your code and content are never exposed publicly and never leave People Work’s controlled infrastructure. <br/><br/>We treat your work with more respect than Ariel treats his Figma files, which says a lot, because those require emotional preparation and a strong coffee before opening.</div></div></div><div class="w-layout-vflex sidebar-slide" id="rights"><div class="stack gap-06"><h2 class="heading-h5">4. Your Rights &amp; How to Manage Your Data</h2><div class="text-medium">You remain fully in control of your data at all times. You can request access, export, correction, or deletion of your information whenever you like. You can remove uploaded files, limit processing for sensitive materials, or delete your account entirely. When you do, People Work removes your personal data and analysis artifacts unless retention is legally required. There are no penalties for leaving. People Work will let you go calmly and professionally. Ariel might take it personally if you stop using his templates, but that is between him and his therapist. <br/><br/>Your code, content, and all outputs generated by People Work remain yours. Always. We do not claim ownership, reuse your work, or quietly admire your structure while pretending it was our idea. People Work only processes what you choose to provide and exists to support your work, not extract value from it. <br/><br/>If you have questions about this policy or how your data is handled, contact us. A real human will respond. Possibly tired. Definitely honest.</div></div></div></div></div></div></div></section></main><section class="section cta"><div class="w-layout-blockcontainer container w-container"><div class="w-layout-vflex cta-content"><div class="w-layout-vflex text center narrow" data-gsap-scroll="text"><h2 class="heading-h2">For teams preparing for <em>growth</em>, not hype</h2></div><div class="w-layout-vflex buttons" data-gsap-scroll="fade"><a class="button-primary animated w-inline-block" href="https://108.supply/website/people-work?utm_source=people-work&amp;utm_medium=template&amp;utm_campaign=get-template" target="_blank"><div class="button-label" data-figma-id="12018:4671">Get Template</div><div class="button-rail"><div class="but