 </svg></div></div></div></a></div></div></div><div class="navigation-overlay"></div></div><main class="main"><section class="section page-header"><div class="w-layout-blockcontainer container w-container"><div class="w-layout-vflex section-content"><div class="w-layout-vflex text center narrow" data-gsap-scroll="text"><h1 class="heading-h1">Style Guide</h1><div class="text-medium">A simple, consistent system designed to keep everything clear, balanced, and easy to build on.</div></div></div></div></section><section class="section padding-top-extra-small"><div class="w-layout-blockcontainer container sticky w-container"><div class="w-layout-vflex section-content"><div class="sidebar-layout" data-pin-wrap="true"><div class="sidebar sticky" data-gsap-scroll="fade" id="w-node-_3e3c1105-280a-78d1-39de-36fd39a4d0e6-d72d3f9d"><div class="anchor-nav"><a class="anchor-nav-item w-inline-block" href="#typography"><div>01</div><div class="text-medium">Typography</div></a><a class="anchor-nav-item w-inline-block" href="#colors"><div class="text-medium">02</div><div class="text-medium">Colors</div></a><a class="anchor-nav-item w-inline-block" href="#buttons"><div class="text-medium">03</div><div class="text-medium">Buttons</div></a><a class="anchor-nav-item w-inline-block" href="#inputs"><div class="text-medium">04</div><div class="text-medium">Inputs</div></a></div></div><div class="sidebar-slides" data-gsap-scroll="stagger"><div class="sidebar-slide"><div class="heading-h6">This page shows only a small part of the system behind this template. Everything here is built with structure in mind, where typography, colors, spacing, and components are all connected through a consistent set of variables and reusable classes, so nothing feels random. <br/><br/>To really understand how it works, it’s worth opening the Navigator, exploring the class structure, and checking the variables, because that’s where the logic actually lives. The goal was to create something clean, flexible, and easy to scale, so you can use it as it is or adapt it to your own way of building without fighting the system.</div></div><div class="w-layout-vflex sidebar-slide" id="typography"><div class="stack gap-06" id="data"><h2 class="heading-h5">Typography</h2><div class="text-medium">Typography is the backbone of this template. Each style is defined to create clear hierarchy, improve readability, and keep the layout consistent across all pages. From large display headings to small captions, everything has its place and purpose. Use them as they are, or adapt them to fit your brand.</div></div><div class="grid"><div class="stack gap-07"><div class="heading-h1">Heading H1</div><div class="heading-h2">Heading H2</div><div class="heading-h3">Heading H3</div><div class="heading-h4">Heading H4</div><div class="heading-h5">Heading H5</div><div class="heading-h6">Heading H6</div></div><div class="stack gap-07"><div class="text-large">Text Large</div><div class="text-large strong">Text Large (Strong)</div><div class="text-medium">Text Medium</div><div class="text-medium strong">Text Medium (Strong)</div><div class="text-small">Text Small</div><div class="text-small strong">Text Small (Strong)</div><div class="label">Label</div><div class="caption">Label</div></div></div></div><div class="w-layout-vflex sidebar-slide" id="colors"><div class="stack gap-06" id="data"><h2 class="heading-h5">Colors</h2><div class="text-medium">The color system is built to be practical, not decorative. It’s based on a small set of neutrals for structure and a few accents to bring focus where it matters. Contrast and usability always come first. You’ll find colors for base surfaces, text, borders, and highlights. They are designed to work together out of the box, but you can easily adjust them to match your brand.</div></div><div class="stack gap-06" id="data"><h3 class="heading-h6">Surface</h3><div class="w-richtext"><p>Neutral define space and structure. They are not text colors. They are the surfaces everything sits on.</p><ul role="list"><li>Surface 1 — main page background</li><li>Surface 2 — elevated surfaces (cards, panels)</li><li>Surface 3 — grounded or contrast sections</li></ul><p>If you want a section to feel darker or heavier, use Surface 3. If you want elevation, use Surface 2.To create a dark section: Switch the section to Inverted Mode. No manual color overrides are needed.</p></div><div class="grid _3-columns"><div class="stack gap-04"><div class="color-box"></div><div class="caption">surface 1</div></div><div class="stack gap-04"><div class="color-box surface-2"></div><div class="caption">surface 2</div></div><div class="stack gap-04"><div class="color-box surface-3"></div><div class="caption">surface 3</div></div></div></div><div class="stack stretch gap-06" id="data"><h3 class="heading-h6">Ink</h3><div>Ink defines hierarchy of information. It is used for text, icons, borders, subtle UI elements</div><div class="w-richtext"><p>The scale is consistent in both modes.</p><ul role="list"><li>Ink-1 — primary content</li><li>Ink-2 — secondary text</li><li>Ink-3 — supportive / meta information</li><li>Ink-4 — borders, dividers, quiet details</li></ul><p>All levels are tonal variations of the base ink color, ensuring consistent hierarchy across light and dark layouts</p></div><div class="grid _4-columns"><div class="stack gap-04"><div class="color-box ink-1"></div><div class="caption">ink 1</div></div><div class="stack gap-04"><div class="color-box ink-2"></div><div class="caption">ink 2</div></div><div class="stack gap-04"><div class="color-box ink-3"></div><div class="caption">ink 3</div></div><div class="stack gap-04"><div class="color-box ink-4"></div><div class="caption">ink 4</div></div></div></div><div class="stack stretch gap-06" id="data"><h3 class="heading-h6">Accent</h3><div>Accent colors are used sparingly for key actions, highlights, brand moments. They remain consistent across modes.</div><div class="grid _4-columns"><div class="stack gap-04"><div class="color-box accent-yellow"></div><div class="caption">accent yellow</div></div><div class="stack gap-04"><div class="color-box accent-blue"></div><div class="caption">accent blue</div></div><div class="stack gap-04"><div class="color-box accent-blue-wash"></div><div class="caption">accent blue wash</div></div><div class="stack gap-04"><div class="color-box accent-pink"></div><div class="caption">accent pink</div></div></div></div></div><div class="w-layout-vflex sidebar-slide" id="buttons"><div class="stack gap-06" id="data"><h2 class="heading-h5">Buttons</h2><div class="text-medium">Buttons are designed to be clear and predictable. Primary actions stand out and guide the user forward. Secondary and tertiary buttons support without competing for attention. The goal is simple: users should always know what to do next without thinking.</div></div><div class="stack gap-06" id="data"><h3 class="heading-h6">Primary</h3><div class="w-layout-hflex row stack-on-tablet gap-04"><a class="button-primary animated w-inline-block" href="#"><div class="button-label" data-figma-id="12018:4671">Primary Animated</div><div class="button-rail"><div class="button-circle small accent"><div class="icon small w-embed"><svg fill="none" viewbox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
