-</svg></div></div></div></div></div><div class="w-layout-vflex sidebar-slide" id="inputs"><div class="stack gap-06" id="data"><h2 class="heading-h5">Inputs</h2><div class="text-medium">Inputs are built to feel calm and easy to use. Different states like default, active, and filled help users understand where they are and what’s happening. Everything is kept minimal so forms don’t feel heavy or distracting. Use them as a base and adapt if your project needs something more custom.</div></div><div class="form-block w-form"><form class="form" data-name="Contact Form" data-turnstile-sitekey="0x4AAAAAAAQTptj2So4dx43e" data-wf-element-id="5597efa2-badb-c146-894a-9017fcb5faac" data-wf-page-id="69e1ec92bf0abf2ed72d3f9d" id="wf-form-Contact-Form" method="get" name="wf-form-Contact-Form"><div class="form-fields"><div class="w-layout-vflex field"><label class="label" for="name">Text Field</label><input class="text-field w-input" data-name="Name" id="name" maxlength="256" name="name" placeholder="Placeholder" required="" type="text"/></div><div class="w-layout-vflex field"><label class="label" for="Message">Text Area</label><textarea class="text-field area w-input" data-name="Message" id="Message" maxlength="5000" name="Message" placeholder="Placeholder"></textarea></div><label class="w-checkbox checkbox-field"><div class="w-checkbox-input w-checkbox-input--inputType-custom checkbox"></div><input data-name="Checkbox" id="checkbox" name="checkbox" style="opacity:0;position:absolute;z-index:-1" type="checkbox"/><span class="text-medium strong w-form-label" for="checkbox">Checkbox</span></label></div></form><div class="success-message w-form-done"><div>Thank you! Your submission has been received!</div></div><div class="error-message w-form-fail"><div>Oops! Something went wrong while submitting the form.</div></div></div></div><div class="w-layout-vflex sidebar-slide" id="inputs"><div class="stack gap-06" id="data"><h2 class="heading-h5">GSAP Split Fix</h2><div class="text-medium">When using GSAP split text, some letters or word endings may get visually clipped because the split wrappers create masking and overflow issues. To prevent this, we added a small custom fix that keeps the text rendering clean and avoids those cut-off edges.<br/><br/>Please do not remove these classes, even if they seem unnecessary at first glance. They are important and intentionally used to override this issue:</div></div><div class="heading-h4"><div class="gsap_split_word">gsap_split_word</div></div><div class="heading-h4"><div class="gsap_split_line">gsap_split_line</div></div><div class="text-medium">Without them, split text may break visually and crop parts of letters.</div></div></div></div></div></div></section></main><section class="section cta"><div class="w-layout-blockcontainer container w-container"><div class="w-layout-vflex cta-content"><div class="w-layout-vflex text center narrow" data-gsap-scroll="text"><h2 class="heading-h2">For teams preparing for <em>growth</em>, not hype</h2></div><div class="w-layout-vflex buttons" data-gsap-scroll="fade"><a class="button-primary animated w-inline-block" href="https://108.supply/website/people-work?utm_source=people-work&amp;utm_medium=template&amp;utm_campaign=get-template" target="_blank"><div class="button-label" data-figma-id="12018:4671">Get Template</div><div class="button-rail"><div class="button-circle small accent"><div class="icon small w-embed"><svg fill="none" viewbox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
